.idea
.git
.github
archive
nginx

.dockerignore
.env
.env.example
.golangci.yml
.gitignore

# Local Go caches: the module cache is read-only and the build cache runs to
# gigabytes, so neither belongs in a build context.
.gopath
.gocache
# The local module cache belongs to this checkout, not to the image: the build
# downloads its own. Left in, it would ship hundreds of megabytes of context.
.gomodcache

coverage.txt
*.test

docker-compose*.yml

# Provider credentials live here; the deployment mounts its own copy. Without
# this line every image layer would carry the development keys.
config/llm.yaml

# Build inputs and documentation, not runtime content. docs/docs.go is
# the one exception: it is the swaggo-generated package the REST router
# imports, so it must stay in the build context. Never collapse the
# docs/* pattern and its exception back to a bare `docs` line - that
# drops the package and the image build fails with
# "no required module provides package .../docs".
docs/*
!docs/docs.go
*.zip
.test-out.txt

LICENSE
Makefile
README*
